# Contributing

Report reproducible problems with the CLI version, Ruby version, operating system
and a minimal example. Remove credentials and private data before sharing output.
Discuss substantial interface changes in an issue before implementing them.

Fork the repository, create a branch, and install dependencies with:

    bin/setup

Run the local checks and the network-dependent advisory audit:

    bundle exec rake check
    bundle exec rake audit

The initial tests cover help, version, text output, invalid options, missing
arguments and broken pipes. Add behavioral tests for new features.

Use Conventional Commit titles, for example:

    fix: handle empty input consistently
    docs: clarify installation

Add user-visible changes under Unreleased in CHANGELOG.md. Maintainers may use
the skip-changelog label for dependency updates or changes without user-visible
effects. Keep the pull request focused and describe the checks you ran.

Generated application code, tests and documentation belong to this repository.
Update them directly. Shared maintenance behavior is upgraded through the
ruby-repo-kit dependency, with CI and review for each update.

Participation follows [our code of conduct](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md). Contributions
are licensed under the [MIT license](LICENSE.txt).
